SUMMARY:Design Your Own Mahjong Tiles Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Design Your Own Mahjong Tiles Workshop            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Sunday December 6\, 2026\n10:00 am – 12:00 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    In this hands-on workshop\, participants will design and glaze a set of 4 ceramic Mahjong tiles using underglaze techniques. Guided by artist Joshua Lue Chee Kong\, explore pattern-making\, symbolism\, and personal storytelling through clay. No experience needed. Just bring your stories\, creativity\, and inspiration! \nThen\, join us on Wednesday December 16 from 6:00 – 8:00 pm for a Mahjong Social Night\, where you can view the complete set of community-designed tiles\, play a game of Mahjong\, and take home your tiles. The tiles will be documented as part of the Mahjong Stories Archive\, a collective archive of personal stories connected to Mahjong. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Your ticket includes one workshop and access to the Mahjong Social Night. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $30\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $35\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. This class is non-refundable and non-transferrable\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n                            \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Joshua Lue Chee Kong\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Joshua Lue Chee Kong is a multidisciplinary artist from Trinidad and Tobago based in Toronto. Working across ceramics\, sculpture\, digital media\, and community-focused projects\, he explores how objects carry personal history and cultural identities across geographical boundaries. His practice draws on nostalgia and transforms familiar forms into opportunities for storytelling\, connection\, and belonging. \nIn 2026\, Joshua co-founded DeNarrative Studio with Barry Ling to support people in telling their stories through art. Their Designing Your Own Mahjong Tiles workshop grew out of their own life experiences and familial memories surrounding mahjong tiles\, using the tiles’ long history and physical form as a platform for others to express their stories. \n \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
