SUMMARY:After the Island: Curator Tour
DESCRIPTION:After the Island: Curator Tour            \n                                    \n                                \n                        \n                                                \n                                                        Get Tickets                        \n                                            \n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thursday December 10\, 2026\n6:30 pm – 7:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Join the exhibition curators for a guided exploration of After the Island: Caribbean Canadian Ceramics. \nLed by Joséphine Denis\, Co-Director & Director of Curatorial Initiatives at Black Artists’ Networks in Dialogue (BAND)\, and Sequoia Miller\, Chief Curator & Deputy Director at the Gardiner Museum\, this tour will focus on the artists’ works and consider the dynamic field of Caribbean ceramic practices. \nGain insight into the unique curatorial partnership between BAND and the Gardiner\, and learn more about the artists and artworks featured in the exhibition. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $21\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $25\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About the Exhibition \nAfter the Island: Caribbean Canadian Ceramics considers how artists of the Caribbean diaspora are embracing the medium of ceramics to explore themes of knowledge transfer and the liberatory potential of the clandestine. Through existing and new work by Caribbean Canadian artists PJ Anderson\, Eddy Firmin\, Manuel Mathieu\, and Sharon Norwood\, the exhibition approaches questions of identity\, belonging\, memory\, and cultural continuity through the language of clay. Learn more \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Exhibition Partners\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Presenting Sponsors\n                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Supporting Partners\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Government Support\n                \n                                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Project Partner\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Media Partners\n                \n                                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Thanks To\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/after-the-island-curator-tour-december-10-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
